rag_contexts:
Rima Das (review): We're exposing a structured 'validation_failures' field to clients.

Need to ensure it doesn't leak internal tokens in PII-sensitive flows.

Aisha Patel (author): Validation metadata is redacted by default and can emit a high-level enum + field path.

Full error details are gated behind enterprise telemetry and only returned when 'expose_validation_details' is enabled (opt-in for Private/Dedicated customers).

Evan Thompson (review): Tests look good.

Please add a migration note for existing OpenAI-compat users; the compatibility transport changes headers.

Aisha Patel (author): Added docs/guides/structured-output.md migration section and the SDK helpers to automatically adapt existing calls.
// incremental validation loop (pseudocode)
for chunk in stream {
  accumulate(chunk)
  if schema_validator.check_prefix(accumulated) == FAIL {
    emit(validation_failures)
    if cfg.rewind_on_schema_failure {
      rewind_to_safe_boundary()
      request_repair_subprompt()
      replay_corrected_substream()
    } else {
      close_with_error()
    }
  }
}
// openai_compat header added
X-Redwood-Validation-Meta: {"mode":"strict","status":"ok|error"}
// SDK helper (typescript)
export function withStrictSchema(client, schema, opts = {}) {
  return client.with({ response_format: { schema, strict: true, rewind_on_schema_failure: opts.rewind } })
}
Add runtime streaming JSON Schema validation with optional rewind+retry behavior.

New API knobs: response_format.strict (boolean), response_format.rewind_on_schema_failure (boolean).

Structured validation failures are returned in OpenAI-compat responses under 'validation_failures' when enabled.

See docs/guides/structured-output.md for migration steps.

Risk: additional CPU on streaming paths for prefix validation.

Mitigation: validation is opt-in per-route, fast-path guard to skip allocation when disabled, and a config to only validate on sampled requests.

Rewind path limited to small correction window and capped retries to avoid increased tail latency.

New unit tests for incremental validator, integration tests that repro schema divergence mid-stream, and e2e scenario that exercises rewind+repair against a mocked LLM.

Benchmarks show ~3-7% cpu increase when validation is enabled on 4xA10 routes; disabled-by-default for high-throughput tiers.
prompt-repair flow reviewed by security.

Repair prompts are templated and sanitized; no raw client prompt content is appended to repair requests.

